WEBVTT

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:07.230
<i>When I gaze at the blueness of the skies,
it makes me long to return to unknown lands.</i>

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:14.530
<i>My soul, drawn in by the blueness of the skies,
is being tossed and scattered into the distance.</i>

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.120
<i>The end—the end of the sky.</i>

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.080
<i>At last I've reached it.</i>

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:25.370
<i>My dear child, I await you on Estalucia,
Island of the Astrals.</i>

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:56.150
Everyone, long time no see!

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:58.530
I've heard the rumors about you!

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:02.570
Despite being led by such a young captain,

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:07.450
you've subdued multiple primal beasts
and taken on the Erste Empire, no less...

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.710
You've really made a huge splash!

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.000
We're not that big a deal—

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.920
Oh, that was nothing!

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.670
We're heading for
the Island of the Astrals, after all!

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:21.800
So? You didn't come here
just to flatter us, did you?

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.090
Katalina, pass the salt, will you?

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:28.100
Sorry, Sierokarte, but the thing is...

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:28.100
Thanks.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.890
I'm afraid we don't have the funds
to make it worth your while to do business with us.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:37.690
No problem, I'm not here to make a sale today.
I have a job for you!

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.110
Lyria! This is so delicious!

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.780
A job? What kind?

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:45.200
If you could kindly direct your attention
to this request form for the details...

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.200
Hold up.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.990
First, let's talk money.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.830
Once our captain hears of someone's plight,

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.630
he has a way of taking on the job
without a second thought.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:56.210
Sorry.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:58.590
Well, he wouldn't be Gran otherwise.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:04.260
When you're the captain of a skyfaring crew,
that just won't fly anymore.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.510
I mean, the skies are teeming with scoundrels.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.020
Here we go again!

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:12.690
Why do old men love lecturing so much?

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.690
Who're you callin' an old man?

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:17.270
It's pretty obvious that I'm talking about you!

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.440
Io, Rackam, let's calm down...

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.870
Expenses aren't included.
After subtracting commission...

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:30.040
Is that all?

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:35.170
The clients are residents
of a tiny island, you see,

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:39.800
and this request doesn't seem
to be particularly dangerous.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.170
This is just my own gut feeling, but...

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.720
It just might involve
some kind of primal beast.

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:52.270
Of course, my gut isn't infallible.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:55.140
So if you could think of this
as a genteel service...

00:04:55.900 --> 00:05:00.520
The Knickknack Shack would be happy
to pay for your dinner tonight!

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.110
- A thousand apples! No, four!
- Every bottle of whisky on the shelf there!

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.110
- The special grilled beef sampler plate!
- A fruit tart and a berry danish!

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.660
- Along with garlic pilaf and cheese fries!
- And whatever snacks you've got!

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.990
Hey... Come on.
Haven't any of you heard of restraint?

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:15.330
Plus an orange parfait and lemonade!

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:09.950
Katalina?

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.660
Do you think I can have another one of these?

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.330
S-Sure...

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:17.420
Make sure you don't leave any leftovers!

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.810
Really, it's so good of you to come!

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:36.270
I was certain that no skyfaring crew
would ever come to an island out here.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.560
I'd all but given up hope.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.070
What's it been, two months already?

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:46.610
We started hearing an odd sound
coming from somewhere.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:47.450
Odd sound?

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:49.070
Night and day...

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:52.450
Just when you think it's stopped,
it starts up again.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:54.830
Such an ominous sound...

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.830
It's creepy.

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:02.590
It's got the cattle spooked, too.
They're producing hardly any milk now.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:09.550
It's not like anyone's getting hurt or sick,
but it's just creepy.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.050
You know, not knowing where
it's coming from and all.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:18.440
Which reminds me... A Draph girl
came to the island on a liner two days ago.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.650
A Draph girl?

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.500
Is this the sound they were talking about?

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:42.500
Lyria.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:53.430
I think so.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.980
There's a primal beast on this island.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:01.100
So was that the primal beast's voice just now?

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:04.110
I'm not sure. It feels very far away...

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:07.320
Like something is blocking its presence.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:10.990
Then Sierokarte's gut was on the money.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:14.660
This doesn't seem like an emergency,

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:18.290
but if there's a primal beast involved,
I don't think we can just leave it like this.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:18.910
Right.

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:21.210
We'll need to exercise more caution...

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:23.880
Come on, just give it up!

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.800
It's only a toy sword!

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:27.880
It's not a toy!

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:32.380
I'm gonna use that sword to practice
and become a real skyfarer one day!

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:37.350
Go slow. Watch your back, Gran.

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:41.140
I know.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:45.150
Th-Thank you.

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:48.280
I never dreamed real skyfarers
would come to the rescue.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:52.660
Don't worry about it. Gran's that kind of guy.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:54.780
That's Gran for you!

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:03.250
Good grief, what a hassle.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:08.710
It's pretty deep. I wonder how far it goes...

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:33.400
Are you all right, Gran?

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.320
We're fine!

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:38.450
Jeez, that gave me a heart attack!

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:49.300
Ahh, I feel so much better!

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.840
The villagers wanted you to have this.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:55.260
Thanks! I was absolutely starving!

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:59.760
It's not as serious as I thought.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.470
You knew to do a breakfall, didn't you?

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:07.690
Going to retrieve a kid's toy,
and coming back with an injured person...

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:09.610
Really, that's our Gran for us!

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:13.820
So why were you lying around
in a place like that, lady?

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.820
Call me Aliza.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:18.570
I'm on a journey as part of
my martial arts training.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:21.990
I came to this island just because
something seemed to point me this way.

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:23.290
Good work, guys...

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:26.500
Gran found her.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:27.670
Huh?

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.630
About that sound...

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:33.840
Looks like there's no doubt about it.
The wind is carrying it from underground.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.800
So there is something underground?

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:40.430
We can't just start digging up the whole place.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:42.890
It'd be easier if we could narrow it down...

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.310
Actually...

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:49.730
I might know something about that.

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:56.030
Since everyone on this island's
been creeped out by the weird sound,

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:59.410
I've been poking around,
thinking it could be a monster or something.

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.040
And when I tracked the sound...

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.470
I tried to run away before it saw me,

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:27.270
but I tripped and ended up
sliding down that cliff.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.320
A primal beast...

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:00.590
Found it! There it is!

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:05.010
So they dug themselves in
underneath an obscure island, huh?

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:07.020
Man, the lengths they'll go to...

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:09.690
Lyria!

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:10.560
Are you all right?

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:13.730
Is that the cause?

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:16.570
Dark essence...

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:18.740
No...

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:24.620
I think that dark essence
only works on the primal beast.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:27.120
But because of it,

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.040
the primal beast's cries are so...

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:30.410
Painful.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:34.290
Lyria, are you...

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:37.880
We've been waiting for you!

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:43.220
You fugitives.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:44.300
Pommern!

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:45.640
You know him?

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:49.180
That man's a captain of the Erste Empire,
as well as our enemy.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:55.480
I've been keeping an eye on you
since your arrival to this island, you know.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:59.110
Here we were,
checking the results of our research,

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:02.530
when who should show up
but you fugitives from justice!

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:05.160
Perhaps I'm being rewarded
for my daily good deeds.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:09.410
You're one to talk, always sneaking around
and up to no good!

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.500
What the heck
are you plotting this time, huh?

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:14.670
Stop, there's no need to panic.

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:19.670
The primal beast Tezcatlipoca
will gladly take you on.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:27.010
Stop it! Please, stop it!

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:32.020
Since we've finished collecting the data
on this primal beast,

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:36.360
all that's left to do is let it run berserk.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.650
The Empire's top secret,

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:44.200
the deserter who spirited her away,
Lieutenant Katalina,

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:48.830
and the captain of the fugitive skyfaring crew
that continues to protect them...

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:52.620
Today marks the end for you all!

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:14.140
You need to run, too!

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:17.560
Are you kidding?
I'm past the point of no return!

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:30.490
It's moving!

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:36.750
Evade!

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:44.970
All that's left for you lot
is to vanish along with this island.

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:51.560
Oh, but we'll be sure to retrieve
the top secret girl later on.

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:04.820
Aliza!

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:12.080
It's way too fast.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:16.710
Dark essence.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:18.870
At the base of its neck.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:22.290
It'll stop rampaging if we can destroy that.

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:25.630
If we can somehow get it to stand still...

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.600
It attacked us,
even though it couldn't see us!

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:39.140
Gran!

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:58.250
Wait a second...

00:14:58.250 --> 00:14:59.080
Heat?

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:02.630
Fangs of the Dragon! Talons of the Phoenix!

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:09.930
It stopped!

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:11.470
Lyria!

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.430
Please! I need your help!

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:49.880
Damn!

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:07.900
You're going to be okay.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:15.240
Thy name is Tezcatlipoca.

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:53.570
Rest well.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.740
All signs of dark essence have vanished.

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:00.410
We can surmise that the primal beast
has also been subdued.

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:05.420
Send all of the data
to Agastia's research headquarters.

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:08.130
The prime minister is waiting for it, you know.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:21.720
You have our utmost gratitude.
Thanks to you, everyone can now live in peace.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:23.850
That was great training for me!

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:25.900
Right back at you. Thanks for everything!

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.110
When next we meet in the skies...

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.530
Let's spar together!

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:41.120
Come back any time you want!

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:44.660
We'll treat you to some of our special cheese!

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.300
Anyway...

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:55.970
Gran and his crew were victorious yet again!

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:58.640
As expected of them.

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:03.810
Aren't you going to join
Gran and the others, Rosetta?

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:06.020
For now...

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:12.190
Let's just say it's up to
the whispers of the forest.

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:16.740
How long's it gonna take
to get to the next island?

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:19.820
Well, since the westward currents
are strong at this time of year...

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:21.330
Two days should be enough.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.910
Take a good look at that red star over there.

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:26.710
It works as a beacon in this season.

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.880
<i>Dear Master, how is your lower back
feeling these days?</i>

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:34.460
<i>Keep in mind how old you are
and not overdo it.</i>

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:44.390
I have a lot to write about today.

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:50.560
About Aliza, the villagers and the primal beast.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.570
Good on you for not missing a day, Lyria.

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:58.820
I also tried to write one before,
but it only lasted about a week.

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:03.660
It's because I'm so happy.

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:08.660
To have so many things to write about,
day after day.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:13.920
A lot's happened, huh?

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:16.170
Yes, all kinds of things.

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:20.220
Gran, do you remember?

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:24.970
That girl who was with the Black Knight.

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:27.850
Yeah.

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:31.100
I can't stop thinking about her.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:35.070
Why did she have the same power as me?

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:41.660
Do you think she knows?
Of what this power is...

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:46.700
And why we both have such a power.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:52.460
I'm not sure about the girl...

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:56.630
But the fact that I'm on
this journey right now...

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:01.760
Lyria, it's all thanks to you.

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:07.640
Because you linked your life to mine.

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:12.850
I wanted to follow my father,
to go to the Island of the Astrals,

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:14.020
to become a skyfarer...

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:18.360
But I couldn't find an opportunity
to leave the island.

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:22.610
Meeting you set everything in motion.

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:25.200
Gran...

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:27.990
I'm going to the Island of the Astrals.

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:31.620
And there, I'm going to find out
about my father, about you,

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:35.040
and about this life that links us together.

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:40.130
I'm sure we'll meet that girl again
if we continue to travel.

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:44.010
Next time, let's definitely talk with her.

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:46.510
I'll do everything I can to make that happen.

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:50.850
Okay.

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:56.060
I want to be friends with that girl.

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:06.370
We hereby offer full amnesty
to the crew of the Grandcypher

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:08.530
and would like to propose
a peace negotiation.

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:11.500
The venue shall be at the Albion Citadel.

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:14.960
From, Major General Furias of the Erste Empire.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:16.330
A peace negotiation?

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:19.340
Does that mean they'll stop chasing after us?

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:21.090
Yeah, a likely story!

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:24.050
Looks like it's do-or-die.

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:06.900
Furias has apparently reached out to
the Grandcypher crew to negotiate for peace.

00:23:07.490 --> 00:23:10.360
Oh? In other words, you know...

00:23:10.360 --> 00:23:13.620
I bet Major General Furias
is gonna cause all kinds of trouble, huh?

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:17.000
So? What do you want us to do?

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:17.830
Nothing.

00:23:18.660 --> 00:23:23.750
I'll need them to be capable
of handling an ordeal of this level.

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:26.920
They'll be useless to me, otherwise.

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:30.630
Let's see which path they choose,
and what lies ahead...

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.940
EPISODE 2
THE ALBION CITADEL

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:38.980
Next episode, "The Albion Citadel."
